WEBVTT

00:00.560 --> 00:02.110
Excuse me.

00:02.110 --> 00:03.230
Yes!

00:03.230 --> 00:05.100
I'll be there in just a moment.

00:07.560 --> 00:08.730
Oh...

00:12.250 --> 00:13.790
Welcome!

00:14.480 --> 00:16.600
Feel free to sit right over here.

00:17.800 --> 00:20.650
Hayato-kun, one house blend and one mocha.

00:20.650 --> 00:21.850
Got it.

00:21.850 --> 00:23.330
Sorry it's so busy.

00:23.680 --> 00:25.860
I should've put three of you on this shift.

00:26.280 --> 00:29.860
But I guess this is the result of our 
Cherry Blossom Festival promotion.

00:33.440 --> 00:34.590
What?

00:34.890 --> 00:38.470
I was just thinking that you seem 
more like a café owner now.

00:39.490 --> 00:41.350
Jeez, where'd that come from?

00:42.680 --> 00:46.350
You don't need to worry. 
I can handle it alone.

00:46.350 --> 00:48.280
O-Okay, then...

00:50.030 --> 00:51.930
Looks like you could use a hand!

00:52.530 --> 00:55.640
Huh? Riho-chan, 
didn't you have classes today?

00:55.640 --> 00:59.530
I figured this would happen, 
so I came home early.

01:01.650 --> 01:05.140
All right! Now that I'm here, all is well!

01:05.620 --> 01:07.370
Th-Thanks...

01:07.660 --> 01:11.250
Didn't you say that 
when you worked yesterday?

01:11.550 --> 01:14.760
Oh, I do expect to be paid, of course!

01:14.760 --> 01:16.730
No, that's not what I...

01:16.730 --> 01:19.120
Excuse me, dear. May I order?

01:19.120 --> 01:20.510
Sure!

01:20.810 --> 01:22.640
Sorry for the wait!

01:22.640 --> 01:25.520
Hey, Granny! You came to see us again?

01:25.870 --> 01:27.420
Thank you!

01:44.080 --> 01:46.660
<b></b>The Café Terrace and Its Goddesses

02:58.280 --> 03:00.530
<b>Episode 5: "Day Off"</b>

02:58.320 --> 03:00.530
<b>Episode 5: "Day Off"</b>

02:58.360 --> 03:00.530
<b>Episode 5: "Day Off"</b>

02:58.410 --> 03:00.530
<b>Episode 5: "Day Off"</b>

02:58.450 --> 03:00.530
<b>Episode 5: "Day Off"</b>

02:58.500 --> 03:00.530
<b>Episode 5: "Day Off"</b>

02:58.540 --> 03:00.530
<b>Episode 5: "Day Off"</b>

02:58.580 --> 03:00.530
<b>Episode 5: "Day Off"</b>

02:58.630 --> 03:00.530
<b>Episode 5: "Day Off"</b>

02:58.670 --> 03:00.530
<b>Episode 5: "Day Off"</b>

02:58.720 --> 03:00.530
<b>Episode 5: "Day Off"</b>

02:58.720 --> 03:00.530
Let's eat!

02:58.760 --> 03:00.530
<b>Episode 5: "Day Off"</b>

02:58.800 --> 03:00.530
<b>Episode 5: "Day Off"</b>

02:58.850 --> 03:00.530
<b>Episode 5: "Day Off"</b>

02:58.890 --> 03:00.530
<b>Episode 5: "Day Off"</b>

02:58.940 --> 03:00.530
<b>Episode 5: "Day Off"</b>

02:58.980 --> 03:00.530
<b>Episode 5: "Day Off"</b>

03:01.400 --> 03:04.080
Man, I'm wiped.

03:04.080 --> 03:05.780
I can't even bring myself to eat.

03:05.780 --> 03:08.300
Talk about lousy table manners.

03:08.300 --> 03:10.920
Well, we were busier than usual today.

03:10.920 --> 03:14.320
Kids who've never worked are such slugs.

03:14.320 --> 03:17.620
Hayacchi, if you're 
not gonna eat that, I will!

03:18.300 --> 03:20.730
No! Eat your dinner!

03:20.730 --> 03:22.280
Ugh...

03:22.280 --> 03:23.220
You know, though...

03:23.220 --> 03:25.850
Maybe it's better not to try so hard.

03:25.850 --> 03:29.320
Is it? If he's gonna complain 
that <i>this</i> is too much,

03:29.320 --> 03:31.420
he'll never make it through tomorrow.

03:32.190 --> 03:33.530
No.

03:33.530 --> 03:34.650
I meant you.

03:34.650 --> 03:36.570
Huh? Me?

03:37.120 --> 03:39.280
I'm totally fine!

03:41.730 --> 03:43.050
Well, okay, then.

03:43.050 --> 03:45.620
Hayacchi, gimme your Hamburg steak!

03:53.940 --> 03:55.080
Bathroom...

03:57.560 --> 03:58.960
Huh?

04:00.560 --> 04:01.740
Yeah?

04:03.440 --> 04:06.350
What're you doing at this hour?

04:06.870 --> 04:08.990
Aw, what's this?

04:08.990 --> 04:13.310
Did you want to see me 
all defenseless in my pajamas?

04:13.940 --> 04:15.960
Yep, that's right.

04:15.960 --> 04:16.940
Gross!

04:17.370 --> 04:20.970
I was picking photos to post 
on the café's social media.

04:20.970 --> 04:25.110
We need to keep promoting 
and get a lot more people to come.

04:25.530 --> 04:29.700
Oh, yeah. I was thinking of 
making flyers to post around.

04:29.950 --> 04:33.520
It looks like they can print 
a thousand for 2,600 yen,

04:33.520 --> 04:35.460
but would we need that many?

04:35.460 --> 04:38.120
I mean, you might as well go ahead.

04:38.120 --> 04:39.710
We can hand them out anytime.

04:39.710 --> 04:41.960
Yeah, good point.

04:41.960 --> 04:43.920
Okay, I'll get a thousand.

04:43.920 --> 04:48.190
Also, we should probably 
make a stamp card, right?

04:48.190 --> 04:51.560
And when someone fills it up, 
they can get a free dessert,

04:51.560 --> 04:55.530
or a coupon for a free coffee or whatever...

04:55.530 --> 04:56.700
Hey...

04:57.690 --> 05:00.040
Why are you working so hard?

05:00.520 --> 05:02.420
You're a part-timer.

05:12.080 --> 05:16.250
This café... saved me.

05:16.250 --> 05:17.260
Huh?

05:17.260 --> 05:19.080
It's all thanks to Grandma

05:19.620 --> 05:22.910
that I can be who I am now.

05:23.770 --> 05:25.340
Who you are now?

05:25.340 --> 05:26.700
Yes.

05:26.700 --> 05:29.690
So I want to protect the café, 
whatever it takes.

05:30.640 --> 05:33.270
I want to do whatever I can

05:33.270 --> 05:37.420
to bring in even more customers 
than it had when she ran it.

05:41.260 --> 05:44.240
Y'know, I can't have you doing 
less work than I pay you for,

05:44.240 --> 05:47.610
but doing more than I pay you for 
isn't any better.

05:47.950 --> 05:48.760
Huh?

05:49.930 --> 05:51.380
I mean, like...

05:51.820 --> 05:54.240
Just do what's normal.

05:57.000 --> 05:59.670
Just stop this. You look pathetic.

06:00.630 --> 06:02.800
You're an embarrassment.

06:04.380 --> 06:06.570
Are you saying... I'm causing trouble?

06:06.570 --> 06:07.580
Huh?

06:10.120 --> 06:12.890
But I have to work hard,

06:14.430 --> 06:16.630
or no one's going to help.

06:24.860 --> 06:27.260
You think working hard 
makes me look pathetic?

06:27.260 --> 06:28.110
Huh?

06:28.110 --> 06:30.240
You think I'm an embarrassment?!

06:30.620 --> 06:33.290
Who's ever going to help, then?!

06:33.290 --> 06:34.240
Whoa...

06:34.240 --> 06:37.240
What the hell? You having 
an emotional breakdown or what?

06:37.240 --> 06:38.250
But...

06:38.250 --> 06:42.040
Like I told you before, I hate unfairness.

06:42.040 --> 06:45.770
So, what?! Are you saying 
I'm the only one making money?!

06:47.720 --> 06:49.760
I'm just worried about you.

06:50.220 --> 06:53.040
You won't last a year at this pace.

06:53.040 --> 06:53.900
Huh?

06:54.480 --> 06:56.890
I'm the owner of that café.

06:56.890 --> 07:01.190
I might not be that reliable now, 
but I'm going to bring it back.

07:01.550 --> 07:06.300
So you can just live your life 
doing what you want to do.

07:06.300 --> 07:10.070
Not that I'd know, but isn't that 
why you're going to college?

07:11.750 --> 07:15.080
<i>You can just live for yourself.</i>

07:15.790 --> 07:19.580
If there's something 
you want to do, just do it.

07:22.480 --> 07:25.420
I'll look after you.

07:25.420 --> 07:28.630
You can just stay here 
and never worry about a thing.

07:31.250 --> 07:32.500
H-Hey...

07:35.730 --> 07:38.100
Wh-What're you crying for?

07:38.100 --> 07:40.760
Are you seriously having 
an emotional breakdown?

07:40.760 --> 07:43.600
I'm not... It's just dry eyes!

07:43.600 --> 07:45.550
And hay fever!

07:45.550 --> 07:47.860
Not that it matters...

07:51.720 --> 07:56.490
But I'll look after you, 
so you don't have to worry.

08:03.680 --> 08:06.400
Ugh! Don't treat me like a child!

08:06.400 --> 08:08.880
I'm two years older than you!

08:09.650 --> 08:11.550
Well, I'm a Tokyo U student.

08:11.550 --> 08:13.880
Like that matters! You're taking off, anyway!

08:14.250 --> 08:17.600
Well, later. Get to bed.

08:26.970 --> 08:29.400
<i>Hayato-kun...</i>

08:31.590 --> 08:35.850
<i>He might be more reliable than I thought.</i>

08:35.030 --> 08:36.410
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

08:35.030 --> 08:36.410
<b>The one you're waiting
for will come to you

Romance will develop
from a connection at work

No concerns of sickness

Find fortune in an
unexpected place when
moving to a new home</b>

08:36.820 --> 08:38.990
Oh, right. The bathroom.

08:38.990 --> 08:45.560
<i>Is it okay for me... to rely on him, then?</i>

08:47.800 --> 08:52.110
Thanks to all of you, we've been 
getting more customers lately.

08:52.110 --> 08:54.300
To keep this momentum going...

08:54.300 --> 08:57.130
I want to launch an offensive 
with a new strategy

08:57.130 --> 08:59.260
and further increase our spoils of war.

08:59.260 --> 09:00.930
There's that nerd talk again.

09:00.930 --> 09:03.340
We should do periodic events.

09:03.340 --> 09:06.750
Oh, then I could change our 
uniform design every month.

09:06.750 --> 09:08.020
Thanks for the meal.

09:08.400 --> 09:11.480
Hey, Akane-chan, do you have any good ideas?

09:11.820 --> 09:14.330
I'll leave the café business to the owner.

09:14.330 --> 09:16.990
I have other stuff to do.

09:16.990 --> 09:20.520
Oh, yeah... I guess today is our day off.

09:20.520 --> 09:21.990
Exactly.

09:22.640 --> 09:24.100
Good luck!

09:24.880 --> 09:27.930
Does she do something on days off?

09:27.930 --> 09:29.000
Yeah, concerts!

09:29.400 --> 09:32.130
She does guitar and vocals for her band.

09:32.130 --> 09:33.320
Huh...

09:33.320 --> 09:36.060
We've said we wanted to go see her shows,

09:36.060 --> 09:39.140
but she says the band's nothing special, 
so we don't have to.

09:39.140 --> 09:43.360
She won't tell us where they're playing, 
or even what the band's called.

09:43.360 --> 09:44.770
That's right.

09:45.080 --> 09:47.140
Maybe Akane-chan's actually...

09:48.400 --> 09:51.290
engaged in some fishy business on the side...

09:52.500 --> 09:55.320
Ooh, like selling squid? Squid's delicious!

09:55.320 --> 09:56.650
It sure is.

09:57.070 --> 10:00.880
That's stupid. Her band 
probably just isn't that great.

10:00.880 --> 10:03.920
Oh? Were you just imagining something pervy?

10:03.920 --> 10:04.620
No.

10:04.620 --> 10:06.870
By the way, Hayato-kun...

10:07.280 --> 10:09.670
About the café's toaster oven...

10:09.670 --> 10:13.540
It hasn't been working right, 
so we might need to replace it.

10:14.630 --> 10:17.630
<b>Do Not Stack</b>

10:15.000 --> 10:17.630
Well, we're only toasting bread in it,

10:17.630 --> 10:20.260
so the cheapest one should be fine, right?

10:21.340 --> 10:23.890
Since I came into the city for this,

10:23.890 --> 10:25.560
maybe I'll catch a movie or...

10:25.560 --> 10:28.780
Yeah, but Akane-san is so awesome, isn't she?

10:28.780 --> 10:32.270
Yeah, she's a great singer, 
and her guitar playing's amazing, too!

10:32.270 --> 10:34.200
She's gonna be famous one day!

10:34.200 --> 10:36.530
I can't wait for today's concert!

10:37.480 --> 10:40.740
Anyway, which movie should I see?

10:54.170 --> 10:57.440
<i>Breaking out!! It feels like 
the frustration's gonna break me</i>

10:57.440 --> 10:59.930
<i>When they see through the contrast 
and the inferiority complex</i>

10:59.930 --> 11:04.090
<i>What can we ask emotions 
that run in parallel?</i>

11:04.090 --> 11:07.420
<i>What do you wanna do? 
It's out of the question when I feel so foul</i>

11:07.420 --> 11:12.030
<i>I'm sick of it, and I won't ever</i>

11:12.030 --> 11:16.610
<i>Be dishonest with my own voice again, 
it's my standard</i>

11:26.910 --> 11:30.960
<i>Indifferently covering it all up,</i>

11:30.960 --> 11:35.050
<i>In the depths of my twisted heart,</i>

11:35.050 --> 11:40.160
<i>I'd pretend I forgot how to yell</i>

11:40.160 --> 11:45.820
<i>And just wear a hurt expression, 
because why not?</i>

11:45.820 --> 11:50.770
<i>It was more irony than I knew what to do with</i>

11:50.770 --> 11:54.220
<i>Breaking out!! 
The impulse is there in plain sight</i>

11:54.220 --> 11:56.750
<i>I'll embrace the stubborn fool in me that says</i>

11:56.750 --> 12:00.860
<i>Staying holed up inside is just sad</i>

12:00.860 --> 12:04.220
<i>I want to love the problem child 
with the broken emotions</i>

12:04.220 --> 12:08.960
<i>With the highest possible affirmation</i>

12:08.960 --> 12:14.880
<i>And I refuse to run away anymore, 
it's my standard</i>

12:19.830 --> 12:21.870
That was so hype!

12:21.870 --> 12:23.470
I know! That rocked!

12:25.510 --> 12:27.470
Okay, I'm going home.

12:27.470 --> 12:30.720
Aw, why don't you come eat with us for once?

12:30.720 --> 12:34.100
For real. We just put on an awesome show.

12:34.100 --> 12:37.740
Sorry. I promised to always 
eat dinner with my family.

12:38.570 --> 12:41.020
Huh? But it's already nine.

12:41.020 --> 12:42.940
She's eating with her family this late?

12:48.870 --> 12:49.910
Yo.

12:50.330 --> 12:52.660
Come with me to buy stuff for dinner.

12:54.010 --> 12:55.170
Wha...

12:55.480 --> 12:58.420
What are you doing here?

12:58.420 --> 13:02.380
I came to buy a toaster oven, and I was 
gonna watch a movie while I was in town,

13:02.380 --> 13:04.650
but none of them looked that good.

13:04.650 --> 13:05.930
So I thought, for a change,

13:06.240 --> 13:10.010
I'd catch a performance by 
an indie band I'd never seen before.

13:10.360 --> 13:12.810
Never thought it'd turn out to be your band.

13:13.480 --> 13:16.480
Let's go. We need to get back soon,

13:16.480 --> 13:18.760
or Ami might starve to death.

13:20.070 --> 13:20.730
Wa...

13:21.200 --> 13:22.680
Wait, Hayato!

13:23.520 --> 13:26.610
You... s-saw the show?

13:26.610 --> 13:28.960
Huh? Of course I did.

13:28.960 --> 13:31.330
I wouldn't pay to get in and then just leave.

13:31.980 --> 13:35.390
You really suck at talk breaks, 
you know that?

13:36.040 --> 13:40.040
I just... wasn't at my 
best today, that's all.

13:40.350 --> 13:43.210
Oh, I was kinda surprised, though.

13:43.210 --> 13:44.170
About what?

13:44.170 --> 13:48.330
You go through your life with some 
pretty passionate thoughts, huh?

13:48.330 --> 13:50.300
I couldn't believe it 
when I heard those lyrics.

13:50.620 --> 13:52.890
God, I want to die...

13:52.890 --> 13:56.270
Why? I'm not making fun of you or anything.

13:57.370 --> 13:59.940
Shut up. Don't talk to me.

13:59.940 --> 14:01.790
You don't get it.

14:01.790 --> 14:04.940
No need to worry. I won't tell the others.

14:05.380 --> 14:06.820
You wouldn't...

14:06.820 --> 14:09.240
I just told you I won't.

14:11.040 --> 14:14.300
Wait! Why do you look so happy, anyway?

14:14.300 --> 14:18.090
Well, I don't get many opportunities 
to push your buttons like this.

14:18.090 --> 14:19.580
I hate you!

14:20.160 --> 14:22.840
Ami-chan's near death again.

14:22.840 --> 14:28.840
That's the battery saver mode she goes into 
when her charge drops below 20%, apparently.

14:23.530 --> 14:28.840
Beep... Beep... Beep...

14:29.270 --> 14:32.970
Why don't you want them to know, anyway?

14:33.310 --> 14:36.980
The other girls were saying 
they wanted to see your show.

14:36.980 --> 14:38.380
No way.

14:38.380 --> 14:41.230
It'd feel like Parents' Day at school. 
Too embarrassing.

14:41.230 --> 14:44.030
Hmm, would it really?

14:44.030 --> 14:45.230
Yes, it would.

14:45.740 --> 14:48.940
It's a good thing to have a dream, though.

14:49.910 --> 14:55.950
I'll do my best to keep the café afloat 
until you can make a living as a musician.

14:57.650 --> 14:59.750
It's nothing that special.

15:00.740 --> 15:01.710
Oh?

15:01.710 --> 15:04.280
I'm only in the band to play around.

15:04.280 --> 15:06.030
Just to kill time.

15:06.030 --> 15:07.260
Really?

15:07.260 --> 15:09.930
Yes. Anything would work.

15:10.420 --> 15:12.760
Nothing I do has any meaning, anyway.

15:13.510 --> 15:16.260
I know that better than anyone.

15:20.560 --> 15:22.010
You're lying.

15:22.010 --> 15:23.150
Huh?

15:23.420 --> 15:25.520
Someone who didn't take music seriously

15:25.520 --> 15:28.530
couldn't move people's 
hearts with their songs.

15:29.090 --> 15:32.530
What? How would you know that?

15:32.530 --> 15:34.030
Because...

15:34.030 --> 15:37.450
It moved <i>my</i> heart, at the very least.

15:37.450 --> 15:40.920
I ended up buying your CD, of all things.

15:42.100 --> 15:45.830
You didn't have to do that for me.

15:45.830 --> 15:46.880
Don't be dumb.

15:47.440 --> 15:49.790
There's no telling 
what'll happen with the café.

15:49.790 --> 15:53.010
Why would I waste money on 
something that had no meaning?

15:56.280 --> 15:59.670
I see. Glad to hear it, then.

16:01.100 --> 16:05.080
But seriously, you need to 
get better at talk breaks.

16:05.720 --> 16:06.730
That's—

16:06.730 --> 16:09.710
And your band name has no impact.

16:09.710 --> 16:12.970
Wouldn't something like 
"Mussy Mustache Girls" be better?

16:12.970 --> 16:14.600
No, it wouldn't!

16:14.990 --> 16:18.620
<b>Hououji Akane Is Curious!</b>

16:14.990 --> 16:19.040
<b>Loiter...</b>

16:15.620 --> 16:19.040
<i>Hououji Akane Is Curious!</i>

16:19.200 --> 16:20.870
<b>Loiter...</b>

16:21.000 --> 16:22.750
<b>Sneak Sneak...</b>

16:24.040 --> 16:26.000
That CD you bought...

16:26.640 --> 16:28.440
Which song did you like the most?

16:28.440 --> 16:31.060
Save it for later! I'm busy right now!

16:32.170 --> 16:34.180
<b>One Week Later...</b>

16:34.640 --> 16:36.090
What?!

16:36.090 --> 16:38.720
You put the kotatsu away?!

16:38.720 --> 16:41.320
Well, it <i>is</i> almost May.

16:41.320 --> 16:43.350
But it's still cold sometimes!

16:43.630 --> 16:46.360
Ami, it's warm on the veranda.

16:46.360 --> 16:47.480
Really?!

16:47.480 --> 16:48.920
Don't you have school?

16:48.920 --> 16:51.230
Today's the school's anniversary!

16:51.230 --> 16:55.240
Kiku-chan and I don't have 
classes today, either.

16:55.240 --> 16:58.190
Oh, you're all off for the day, too?

16:58.190 --> 16:59.680
So am I.

16:59.680 --> 17:01.770
By the way, where's Hayato-kun?

17:01.770 --> 17:06.310
Since the café's closed today, he went 
to buy coffee filters and other stuff.

17:04.870 --> 17:07.500
<b>Traffic Safety</b>

17:04.870 --> 17:07.500
<b>Traffic Safety</b>

17:07.500 --> 17:10.190
It's so nice out!

17:10.190 --> 17:11.250
Sure is.

17:12.770 --> 17:14.570
It's so peaceful.

17:15.880 --> 17:17.510
Oh, that's right!

17:18.700 --> 17:21.640
It's the pumpkin cheesecake 
that didn't sell yesterday.

17:21.640 --> 17:23.180
Looks great!

17:23.520 --> 17:27.720
Well, Kiku-chan's the only one who 
can make the cakes Grandma made.

17:29.300 --> 17:31.690
Wait... Cheesecake...

17:31.690 --> 17:33.430
Hey, Shiragiku-san...

17:33.850 --> 17:36.200
Do you like blue cheese, too?

17:36.520 --> 17:39.700
Huh? I mean, I don't mind it...

17:40.000 --> 17:42.020
Why? 'Cause it stinks?

17:42.470 --> 17:43.700
Cut it out.

17:44.040 --> 17:46.780
Still, it's been a month and a half 
since we reopened.

17:47.170 --> 17:49.920
I'm glad it seems like 
we'll be able to get by.

17:49.920 --> 17:55.920
I was so worried when Hayato-kun 
first told us to move out.

17:56.400 --> 18:00.300
Well, I guess he's doing his best 
as owner, in his own way.

18:01.030 --> 18:04.310
His coffee still needs some work, though.

18:04.950 --> 18:06.560
Hey, Shiragiku-san...

18:06.560 --> 18:08.940
Do you like kusaya and durian?

18:08.940 --> 18:10.570
Huh? Why do you ask?

18:10.570 --> 18:11.260
'Cause they sti—

18:11.260 --> 18:12.570
Ami-chan!

18:12.570 --> 18:16.570
But you know, Hayato-kun 
really is weird, isn't he?

18:16.570 --> 18:18.010
How so?

18:18.010 --> 18:23.080
I mean, he lives with all these 
cute girls, and he's not even fazed!

18:23.080 --> 18:27.460
I think he's just more concerned 
about the café.

18:27.460 --> 18:31.460
But he saw me naked!

18:31.800 --> 18:36.460
You sure that wasn't your fault 
for walking in when the light was on?

18:36.930 --> 18:40.080
But the "bath in use" sign wasn't up!

18:40.080 --> 18:41.420
Your Honor!

18:41.420 --> 18:43.720
He saw me naked, too!

18:44.930 --> 18:48.480
Because you ignored the "bath in use" sign 
and walked in anyway.

18:49.600 --> 18:52.860
I don't know about any of that...

18:53.200 --> 18:56.510
But Hayato-kun is a guy, after all.

18:56.510 --> 18:58.860
If a girl came on to him,

18:59.280 --> 19:01.820
he might actually get into it.

19:07.680 --> 19:09.480
I think we'll be fine.

19:09.480 --> 19:10.360
Agreed.

19:10.360 --> 19:12.030
It'll never happen.

19:12.030 --> 19:13.290
R-Really?

19:13.290 --> 19:17.830
Shiragiku-san, you like the smell 
of your dad's socks, right?

19:17.830 --> 19:18.700
What?!

19:18.700 --> 19:20.800
No, of course I don't!

19:20.800 --> 19:22.030
But they sti—

19:22.030 --> 19:23.050
Stop it!

19:23.420 --> 19:27.060
Hey, can I bring up 
something totally unrelated?

19:27.060 --> 19:28.250
Huh?

19:28.250 --> 19:33.310
My friend's band is thinking of changing 
their band name. What do you think?

19:33.310 --> 19:34.830
Changing the name?

19:34.830 --> 19:36.320
To what?

19:37.480 --> 19:39.340
Mussy Mustache Girls.

19:43.610 --> 19:45.880
Uh... I don't know.

19:45.880 --> 19:48.080
I do think it'd be easy to remember...

19:48.080 --> 19:51.330
You mean... something like this?

19:52.200 --> 19:55.340
I'll tell her the current name is fine.

19:56.370 --> 19:58.860
Anyway, you know...

19:58.860 --> 20:02.890
He said he'd quit if we 
didn't get results within a year,

20:02.890 --> 20:07.600
but what do you think he'll do 
if the café just... keeps going?

20:07.600 --> 20:12.310
I don't know. It's not like we can 
stay here forever, anyway.

20:12.590 --> 20:15.660
I guess he'd hire new part-time workers,

20:15.660 --> 20:17.830
or get married and have his wife...

20:19.450 --> 20:22.970
M-Married?! Who's Hayato-kun gonna marry?!

20:22.970 --> 20:24.030
Well...

20:24.520 --> 20:28.030
I-I definitely wouldn't want 
to marry a guy like him!

20:28.380 --> 20:30.640
Yeah, same here.

20:30.640 --> 20:34.920
He has no respect for 
his elders, for one thing.

20:35.230 --> 20:39.670
I've... never even thought about that, but...

20:39.980 --> 20:44.680
Well, I like Hayacchi! 
He plays with me sometimes!

20:44.680 --> 20:47.440
And he shares his food with me!

20:47.440 --> 20:49.360
You think like a dog.

20:49.360 --> 20:51.560
Does he think of her as a pet?

20:51.560 --> 20:53.480
Anyway, I can't see it.

20:53.480 --> 20:54.940
Yeah, not a chance.

20:55.210 --> 20:58.470
I don't think he could ever get married.

20:59.440 --> 21:02.740
I might be willing to do it.

21:12.950 --> 21:14.410
Just kidding.

21:15.030 --> 21:18.090
Wait, about what?! 
Which part were you kidding about?!

21:18.090 --> 21:20.420
Were you always the type 
to make jokes like that?!

21:20.840 --> 21:21.930
Surprised you?

21:21.930 --> 21:23.240
Seriously, which part?!

21:23.240 --> 21:25.130
Well, as for me...

21:26.000 --> 21:31.720
I'm gonna protect this town 
with Hayacchi someday!

21:32.110 --> 21:35.440
The next time any bad guys attack, I'll...

21:35.440 --> 21:37.100
Hey, you guys.

21:37.100 --> 21:38.460
I bought cake...

21:41.090 --> 21:42.250
Dosukoi!

21:54.520 --> 21:57.870
Come on. Don't make that scary face.

21:57.870 --> 22:00.220
Wanna stick something in between?

22:02.700 --> 22:06.010
What the hell are you thinking?!

22:06.010 --> 22:07.390
Take this!

22:07.390 --> 22:09.210
Dosukoi!

22:09.210 --> 22:11.210
Another peaceful day...

23:41.980 --> 23:56.990
<b>Episode 6: "Two Months!"</b>

23:41.980 --> 23:56.990
<b>Episode 6: "Two Months!"</b>

23:42.720 --> 23:44.690
Huh? What's this CD?

23:44.690 --> 23:46.920
Oh, it's from Akane's—

23:47.860 --> 23:50.330
There's a guitar pick lodged 
in Hayato-kun's forehead!

23:50.330 --> 23:52.720
That's a cursed CD.

23:52.720 --> 23:53.390
Huh?!

23:53.390 --> 23:55.990
If you listen to it, you'll die. 
Like Hayato just did.
